eak/UI/Front/Row/03%20Bottom/01%20Octave/Button/Up/","source-block-707","Microfreak/UG/03 Overview/01 Front Panel/03 Bottom Row/01 Octave Select",["Octave Up button","Source"]],["Microfreak/UI/Front/Row/03%20Bottom/01%20Octave/Button/Up/Asset/Panel/png/","source-block-43","Octave Up button on the panel",[]],["Microfreak/UI/Front/Row/03%20Bottom/01%20Octave/Button/Up/Asset/Panel/png/","source-block-248","Cropped from Microfreak/UG/03 Overview/01 Front Panel/03 Bottom Row/Asset/01-Bottom-row-of-the-MicroFreak/png.",["Octave Up button on the panel"]],["Microfreak/UI/Front/Row/03%20Bottom/01%20Octave/Ref/Key%20Range/","source-block-229","Octave key range reference",[]],["Microfreak/UI/Front/Row/03%20Bottom/01%20Octave/Ref/Key%20Range/","source-block-260","The notes the MicroFreak's 25 keys send at each octave shift, from -3 to +3, as the Microfreak/UI/Front/Row/01 Top/04 OLED shows it. Note names follow Music/Concept/Scientific Pitch Notation, where MIDI note 60 is C4, middle C. MIDI note numbers are in parentheses.",["Octave key range reference"]],["Microfreak/UI/Front/Row/03%20Bottom/01%20Octave/Ref/Key%20Range/","source-block-537","When the OLED shows -1",["Octave key range reference"]],["Microfreak/UI/Front/Row/03%20Bottom/01%20Octave/Ref/Key%20Range/","source-block-566","The lowest key sends C2 (36), the C in the middle of the keyboard sends C3 (48), and the highest key sends C4 (60), middle C.",["Octave key range reference","When the OLED shows -1"]],["Microfreak/UI/Front/Row/03%20Bottom/01%20Octave/Ref/Key%20Range/","source-block-696","Arturia's manual and Ableton/Live name the same three notes C1, C2 and C3.",["Octave key range reference","When the OLED shows -1"]],["Microfreak/UI/Front/Row/03%20Bottom/01%20Octave/Ref/Key%20Range/","source-block-779","Every octave",["Octave key range reference"]],["Microfreak/UI/Front/Row/03%20Bottom/01%20Octave/Ref/Key%20Range/","source-block-798","The center key is the C in the middle of the keyboard, the 13th key from the left.",["Octave key range reference","Every octave"]],["Microfreak/UI/Front/Row/03%20Bottom/01%20Octave/Ref/Key%20Range/","source-block-1448","Arturia and Ableton octave numbers",["Octave key range reference"]],["Microfreak/UI/Front/Row/03%20Bottom/01%20Octave/Ref/Key%20Range/","source-block-1489","Arturia's manual and Ableton Live name MIDI note 60 C3, so each of their octave numbers is one below scientific pitch notation. The MicroFreak 5.0 manual gives the full MIDI range, notes 0 to 127, as C−2 to G8 in Microfreak/UG/06 Dig Osc/01 as Soundgen.",["Octave key range reference","Arturia and Ableton octave numbers"]],["Microfreak/UI/Front/Row/03%20Bottom/01%20Octave/Ref/Key%20Range/","source-block-1753","Sources",["Octave key range reference"]]],"format_version":5}